MDL408, G8: routines takes no value, so GLib parses the value "-t" as the short
option of threads, which takes the next element of the vector, "--outputdir",
as its value: "Cannot parse integer value", and mydumper aborts at startup.
-- scenario --
tool: mydumper
versions: >= v0.19.1-1
args: --defaults-file /work/mydumper.cnf --host mysql --user e2e --password e2e-password --database app
lint: MDL408
expect config-loaded: true
expect exit: nonzero
expect stderr-contains: Cannot parse integer value
expect stderr-contains: for -t
-- mydumper.cnf --
[mydumper]
routines=-t
outputdir=/work/dump
